I did items 1 to 5 and checked item 6, which needed no change. One side effect needs your decision: `slack.com/help` is now blocked by default (details under item 1). `npm test` passes: 50/50 worker tests and 40/40 extension tests (38 before, plus the 2 I added). `npx tsc --noEmit` in `worker/` is clean. Nothing was committed, and your earlier uncommitted edits are still in the tree.

**Files changed:** `extension/lib/blocklist.js`, `extension/lib/redact.js`, `extension/manifest.json`, `extension/test/privacy.test.mjs`, `worker/src/index.ts`.

1. **Done.** In `matchOne`, a pattern like `*.okta.com` now matches `okta.com` itself as well as its subdomains. It does not match `notokta.com`. I added a test for this.
   - **Behaviour change:** the default list includes `*.slack.com`, so `https://slack.com/help/...` is now blocked. The existing "allows ordinary reading" test expected it to be allowed, so I removed that URL from the test. If you want Slack's public help pages captured again, I can add an exception for `slack.com`.
2. **Done.** Redaction now strips Cloudflare tokens starting with `cfut_`, `cfat_` or `cfct_`, using the same pattern as `secret-guard.mjs`. The new test builds the fake tokens from string pieces, like the existing tests do.
3. **Done.** The CSP now says `object-src 'none'`. `scripts/build-firefox.mjs` copies the Chrome manifest with `structuredClone` and doesn't change the CSP, so the Firefox build gets the same value.
4. **Done.** `/api/verify` now uses the trimmed `GHOST_SECRET` for the proof, matching `verifyBearer`. That is the only place `verifyProof` is called.
5. **Done, without a test.** `authorised()` now reports whether the request used the header or `?token=`. When it was `?token=`, the `/mcp` response is sent without CORS headers. Header auth keeps the current CORS headers. No existing test file covers `index.ts` or CORS, so I skipped the test as you said.
6. **Confirmed, no change needed.** `ingestPages` adds exactly one result for each input page, in input order, on every path: skipped, created, merged (with or without rewriting chunks), updated, and error. There is no "blocked" status in the Worker. So matching results to the batch by position in `doSync` is correct.
